      "content": "You're on the right track, and the materials you're looking for are typically referred to as \"electromyography shielding\" or \"EMG shielding\" materials. These materials can effectively block or dampen the GSR and HRV signals, ensuring a more neutral data profile. Some effective options include conductive fabrics, such as copper or silver-coated fabrics, or even a thin layer of insulating materials like silicone or vinyl. You could also consider applying a thin layer of conductive paint or a specialized EMG shielding spray to the chair's contact points.",
      "source": "target",
